  <layout>One page of verse, set in italic type, in one block. Running head centred at the top, page number at the top right. Signature mark at the lower right, below the last line.</layout>
  <page_number>65</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Milesve tantum perdere principem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Tentauit, eheu! sub duce Barbaro</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Gallus? Tyrannorumq; signa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Hospita Guisiadum sequutus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Funesta Gallis praelia ciuibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Impune monuit? Ruraq; feruido</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Sulcata Francorum labore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Marte suo populata vidit?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Quum sceptra Genti Gallica perfidæ, Et fraudulento prodidit hospiti:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Quum iussa vellet subiugatos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Francigenas Lotharinga ferre?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Tali superbis milite, Guisie,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Regnumq; poscis, quidlibet impotens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Sperare, per vastas ruentis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Dum patria furit ille cædes.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Sic regna stirpi debita regiæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Galloq; captas aduena principi?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Sic prisca Legum sacra turbas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Et Salicæ pia iura Normæ?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Te blandienti somnus imagine,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Te mentis error ludit amabilis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Quum sceptra Gallorum lacertis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Grandia non paribus prehensas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Qui regna terris diuidit omnibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Qui regna firmat legibus additis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Tremendus author, Gentibusque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Iura dedit, violanda nulli:</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>E. j</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <notes>The first line reads "Milesve" with a small mark over the e that may be a printed superscript; I read it as printed. Line 1 may begin with a superscript letter in the original. Otherwise the text is clear. Stanza divisions are not visible in the layout, so the verse is given as one paragraph with its lines kept.</notes>
